|description2=
* Fastest followup, can be plus on block depending on timing and tends to trade with or beat defensive air-to-airs.
* Very good if timed to be meaty, but it's easily reaction DP'd with no way to mix it up meterlessly.
* Has significant landing recovery, so it can't be made safe against most reversals.

Primary hit followup, with no significant difference between versions. Puts a massive hitbox in front of Andy that's basically always going to keep him safe if it connects, so it's good as a safety net when doing 214B in neutral to bait out responses. It will usually beat or favorably trade with people trying to air-to-air in response to the flip, though the hitbox doesn't go as high as it looks, so some can jump over it. Gives a massive launch on air counterhit, which again, isn't too uncommon, and on grounded hit it's also Andy's highest damage starter.

It can be very plus as a meaty hit, and it's also an overhead, but good luck trying to take advantage of that when so much of the cast can DP an obviously close flip at no cost or risk and it cannot be mixed up with a low hit on the same frame.
}}
