|description2=
* Hilariously active low slide. A very powerful meaty, and can easily be spaced in neutral to be safe or plus.
* In meaty setups, Andy can do an empty flip to bait reversals intended to beat slide.
* Can be mixed up with B, an overhead, but this is fuzzy blockable or DP'able.

While it is a low out of Demon Flip, this move is really more of a harrass tool and a + on block meaty than any kind of mixup, as it's not possible to hit this on the same frame as Flip B, and even on timings that come close, a DP beats both AND empty flip. In setups that have the slide hit meaty however, not only is it a good starter and reliably +, Andy is usually going to be able to empty flip and bait reversals, do a different meaty, or simply throw the opponent, so this is probably meterless slide's best application.

Ironically, EX slide is actually more niche, as it's less + on block and a weaker starter and cannot be spaced in neutral, though with the added threat from EX flip's other options, it will probably more frequently catch people off guard as a low. Even if the opponent can react, Flip C makes a reaction DP risky, so it will likely just get blocked, where it has excellent blockstun for Rev Cancels, if not for a raw connect.
