Similar to Flip D, it's a bit challenging to use the meterless versions as mixup; you need the opponent to not react with a DP or to not have one at all in order to push any kind of mix between this and Flip B. However, this move is similarily good in neutral since it just straight up beats high dodge and even some late brakeable DP's, since they're not immune to throws. If the opponent relies on these options and isn't ready to commit a fully invicible reversal to anti-air, this can be a very rewarding way to get in on them, since it's a hard knockdown.

To that end, doing the appropriate meterless version is better, as EX actually does less damage but has the same knockdown. EX Flip Grab is more rewarding on hit if you have resources however, and it can actually be a mixup thanks again to Flip C. And while it will lose to crouch, it will beat anti-airs all the same, so it can be a more brainless tool to accomplish what the meterless ones do, and potentially nuke their HP while at it.
