==Super Special Moves==
====Zan'ei Shouha Ken====
{{FrameDataCargo-COTW
|moveId=andy_236236a,andy_236236c
|input=236236A/C
|captions=<br>Attack animation,<br>C super flash
|description2=* Only the C version is invincible and can be braked.
* Neither version has exceptional range, but they're both easy to combo into.
* 236236A is generally Andy's best use of meter, it has good damage and corner carry.
* 236236C is maybe Andy's best reversal and still an okay combo ender.
* 236236C can be braked halfway through. Links into cl.D on counter hit or wild punish.
Your best friend for meter usage. 236236A is fast, does high damage and always leads to an identical knockdown, so Andy can always get his preferred setups from it, so long as the spacing is right. Even midscreen, the corner carry is huge and you still get to run oki after. For all of this, it's the best in basically every situation where invulnerability isn't needed, and is still preferred as a guard cancel.

236236C is significantly rarer to see, as not only does it do less damage for its cost, but also has a worse knockdown. Its main selling points are being Andy's best metered reversal (or at least the most reliable), and being brakable halfway through, leading to a combo, which has its situational uses. For max damage punishes this just isn't the way to go, but as a starter (usually as a reversal), it keeps the opponent grounded when braked, letting Andy followup with a full heavy to heavy confirm for over 50% damage in S.P.G. so long as he has Rev to spare, off of what is a really strong reversal. Also, these combos refund some of its cost in the process, so they're straight up more economic than the full super.

Interestingly, Andy can perform a "pseudo-236236C" by doing 236AC~6C > 623AC > 214AC, or 236AC~6C > 623AC~AB for the braked version. This visually resembles 236236C, but deals less damage and fills up the REV gauge instead of depleting meter. Hilariously, this means he can "perform" this super twice in one combo.
}}

====Chou/Zetsu Reppa Dan====
{{FrameDataCargo-COTW
