|description2=* Both version are invincible.
*Due to the slow startup, neither version is particularly good as a wakeup reversal, though they can definitely work.
*They both hit quite high and far, which actually gives them some utility in neutral as fireball punishes and they are preferred in a few pickups.
*236236B has a situational use as a combo ender due to giving better frame advantage than 236236A and thus enabling much better mid screen okizeme in exchange for a little damage.

The two versions are almost entirely identical with 236236D simply being higher damage with a better hitbox. Not great as wakeup supers, but if you want to gamble regardless, this is your main option. Considering the slow startup but enormous hitbox, both of these supers are actually better used as long range anti-airs, whiff punishes, or anti-fireball options.
}}

==Hidden Gear==
====Zetsu Tougai Narashi====
{{FrameDataCargo-COTW
|moveId=andy_236236REV
|display=150x150px
|description= * Resets the Rev meter to 0%, even during Overheat. Only available during S.P.G.
*Very weird compared to most Hidden Gears, usually won't hit on its first active frame on grounded opponents which can hurt it as a reversal.

Hidden Gear with an unusual attack animation and hitbox, which ironically makes it one of the most limiting ones in the game. Frequently not hitting on the first frame and its strange hitbox make it unreliable as a reversal, and its knockdown is fairly weak as well, so the best you'll get is f.C as a late meaty or 214C to poke from range, which are unrewarding and potentially unsafe. Suffice to say, your meter is generally better spent on 236236A, however when you do use this as a combo ender, combined with Andy's monstrous punish damage, you are likely winning the round off that combo alone.
}}

